	<version major="4" minor="6" revision="0" build="1" lslib_meta="v1,bswap_guids,lsf_keys_adjacency" />
	<region id="TimelineContent">
		<node id="TimelineContent">
			<attribute id="CompilationTimeStamp" type="int64" value="1706623538" />
			<children>
				<node id="Effect">
					<!--Start Dialog Tutorial Edits-->

					<!--This file will break down the different sections of the dialog timeline file, along with some common effect components! I'll be marking sections with my notes and edits with 'Start Dialog Tutorial Edits', like the other files, and ending them with 'End Dialog Tutorial Edits.'
					
					Effect components annotated in this file (not all of them are edited, but I did put notes about them here!):
					
					> TLVoice
					> TLEmotionEvent
					> TLAttitudeEvent
					> TLAnimation
					> TLSwitchStageEvent
					> TLShowWeapon
					> TLShowPeanuts
					> TLShot

					And, again, I'll be explaining the basic elements of the timeline, as well. Starting with the Duration of the timeline:-->

					<!--The total duration of the timeline. Make sure you update this for anything you add!-->
					<attribute id="Duration" type="float" value="1238.046" />
					<children>
                        <!--The Phases section lists out information about each "Phase" in the timeline. A "Phase" refers to one section of the timeline, that contains everything needed to play for a given line of dialog, cinematic, or set of grouped dialog. These need to be in the same order as the PhaseIndexes for the dialog! Putting them out of order will prevent them from playing. I'll be explaining more about PhaseIndexes later in this file.-->					
						<node id="Phases">
							<children>
								<!--The first phase in the timeline.-->
								<node id="Phase">
									<!--The duration of that phase. Make sure this is updated if any changes in the length of a phase were made!-->
									<attribute id="Duration" type="float" value="18.29" />
									<!--This is almost always 1!-->
									<attribute id="PlayCount" type="int32" value="1" />
									<!--The UUID of the dialog node in the DialogsBinary file. For grouped dialog, this would be the GroupID.-->
									<attribute id="DialogNodeId" type="guid" value="a6ff1d39-25a0-909e-4eda-f7de5eaaf3f7" />
                                    <!--I'll be honest, I'm not sure what this does. Almost every dialog file I've looked at had this present in every phase entry, but had "QuestionHoldAutomation" set to False in the TimelineSettings section. So. [shrugging sounds]-->
									<children>
										<node id="QuestionHoldAutomation" />
									</children>
								</node>
								<!--You'll need to add a new Phase entry for anything you add to the timeline!-->

								<!--End Dialog Tutorial Edits-->
