								<!--Start Dialog Tutorial Edits-->

								<!--This section will cover TLVoice and TLEmotionEvent!-->

								<!--I won't be editing TLVoice here, but I will be going over how it works.
								
								I am, however, going to change Astarion's expression during his line, 'Can't get enough? I'm not surprised' to Surprised, using TLEmotionEvent! Turns out he was surprised, after all.-->

								<node id="EffectComponent">
									<!--TLVoice helps the game reference voice lines from the DialogsBinary files! It doesn't actually reference the audio, lipsyncing, or animation for the line itself; that's handled by the text handle for the line in the DialogsBinary file. That text handle will link to those files through the character's voicebank.
									
									Instead, the TLVoice component helps the game determine when the line should play, what dialog node it's pulling from, and a few other parameters, including tweening for the mocap animations!-->
									<attribute id="Type" type="LSString" value="TLVoice" />
									<attribute id="ID" type="guid" value="6bc1662b-c1ca-4fbe-aca8-7b2ee811c73a" />
                                    <!--The StartTime for the line in the total timeline.-->
									<attribute id="StartTime" type="float" value="419.09778" />
									<!--Often, the end time for TLVoice is shorter than the phase itself, to add padding after voice lines for pauses/etc. This end time is usually based on the duration of the audio file itself.-->
									<attribute id="EndTime" type="float" value="423.89777" />
									<!--The PhaseIndex for the line. This groups together all the different effects needed to play for a given line of dialog. In this case, it's Astarion's 'Can't get enough? I'm not surprised' line when you ask to kiss him.-->
									<attribute id="PhaseIndex" type="int64" value="30" />
									<attribute id="IsSnappedToEnd" type="bool" value="True" />
									<!--This is the UUID of the dialog node for the line in the DialogsBinary file!-->
									<attribute id="DialogNodeId" type="guid" value="47c0a4ba-1d35-11f5-095d-e70a8a7ec073" />
									<!--Sometimes, multiple lines can be included in a single dialog node, which are given their own PhaseIndex and spot on the timeline. This is done by giving the line a unique CustomSequenceID in the DialogsBinary file! That CustomSequenceID will be referenced in the TimelinePhases section (more on that later), and should be used as the ReferenceID here. The Phases section should use the same UUID as the original dialog node, though, and not the CustomSequenceID.
									
									Custom sequences can be used to randomize dialog, like Astarion's kiss reactions, but can also be used to give unique lines for things like pronouns, if the character's speaking to a specific Origin character, etc.
									
									When there's only one possible line for a dialog node, this ReferenceID will be the same as the dialog node UUID.-->
									<attribute id="ReferenceId" type="guid" value="886d508e-0fbe-4ab7-a587-828a92006301" />
									<!--I'll be honest, I'm not totally sure what this does! I couldn't really tell what was changing when I edited it. It doesn't seem to control audio fading or lipsync or animation transitions, so, hm.-->
									<attribute id="PerformanceFade" type="double" value="0" />
									<!--Controls mocap animation tweening/transitioning at the start of the line! This is the amount of time the animation will take to transition be'tween' the previous animation/pose and the one for this line.-->
									<attribute id="FadeIn" type="double" value="0" />
									<!--Same as before, only at the end of the line.-->
									<attribute id="FadeOut" type="double" value="0" />
									<!--Not sure! I couldn't really tell what was changing when I was fiddling with this setting.-->
									<attribute id="HeadPitchCorrection" type="double" value="-0.05235987901687622" />
									<children>
										<node id="Actor">
											<!--The character saying the line. In this case, Astarion, of course!-->
											<attribute id="UUID" type="guid" value="baa8d56b-3671-0f79-04fd-4345329cf311" />
										</node>
									</children>
								</node>


								<!--End Dialog Tutorial Edits-->

								<node id="EffectComponent">
									<attribute id="Type" type="LSString" value="TLAttitudeEvent" />
									<attribute id="ID" type="guid" value="ea1a0318-7c1b-48e4-75fb-e93f7eb02098" />
									<attribute id="StartTime" type="float" value="419.09778" />
									<attribute id="EndTime" type="float" value="423.89777" />
									<attribute id="PhaseIndex" type="int64" value="30" />
									<attribute id="IsSnappedToEnd" type="bool" value="True" />
									<attribute id="IsMimicry" type="bool" value="True" />
									<children>
										<node id="Actor">
											<attribute id="UUID" type="guid" value="0b2d1337-faae-406d-881d-ae38f4777a5f" />
										</node>
									</children>
								</node>
								<node id="EffectComponent">
									<attribute id="Type" type="LSString" value="TLAttitudeEvent" />
									<attribute id="ID" type="guid" value="2730c7f0-2735-4220-b5a4-6f2fc625376f" />
